</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">III. Replay and Execution.</span>
We execute the synthesized instruction <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> from the start state of <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain
an <span id="S3.SS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Execution Sequence</span>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\leftarrow\textsc{ExecuteInstruction}(I)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">ExecuteInstruction</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\leftarrow\textsc{ExecuteInstruction}(I).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This sequence represents how the environment actually responds to the instruction.
Discrepancies between <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> (expected behavior) and <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> (observed outcome)
indicate semantic gaps in <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math>, e.g., missing contextual cues or ambiguity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">IV. Similarity Verification.</span>
To quantitatively measure alignment between the <span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reference</span> and <span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Execution Sequences</span>,
we perform the similarity verification using the <span id="S3.SS2.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action-Level Reconstruction Recall</span> metric:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R(A,B)=\frac{1}{|A_{a}|}\sum_{a\in A_{a}}\mathbf{1}\bigl[\exists b\in B_{a}:\,\mathrm{match}(a,b\mid s)\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.448em">:</mo><mi>match</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A,B)=\frac{1}{|A_{a}|}\sum_{a\in A_{a}}\mathbf{1}\bigl[\exists b\in B_{a}:\,\mathrm{match}(a,b\mid s)\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{match}(a,b\mid s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>match</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{match}(a,b\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnotex6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            The prompt templates used at each stage are provided in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Prompt Summary ‣ HATS: Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis for GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</span></span></span> determines whether executing <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> in state <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>
is semantically equivalent to action <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> in its original context.
A lower <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A,B)</annotation></semantics></math> implies that the instruction <math id="S3.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> lacks critical contextual cues,
for instance, it may omit widget identifiers, temporal dependencies, or navigation context.
We later compare this recall metric with a precision-based alternative in our
metric analysis (§<a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ HATS: Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis for GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">V. Iterative Refinement and Final Verification.</span> If <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A,B)&lt;R_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A,B)&lt;R_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> or execution fails, <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is refined by injecting missing context and re-executed to obtain an updated <span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Execution Sequence</span>.<span id="footnotex8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnotemark"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">footnotemark: </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            </span></span></span> This replay–refine loop continues until alignment improves (<math id="S3.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A,B)\geq R_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A,B)\geq R_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>) or the refinement budget <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> is reached. We set <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\min}=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\min}=0.7</annotation></semantics></math> based on empirical validation balancing stability and coverage. When <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> yields stable, deterministic execution, the pair <math id="S3.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I,B)</annotation></semantics></math> is accepted as a <span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Verified Trajectory</span>. Otherwise, it is discarded, and its misalignment contributes to the <span id="S3.SS2.p7.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">hardness reward</span> for future exploration.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Only verified trajectories that pass alignment verification are admitted to the corpus, ensuring that synthesized data are both <span id="S3.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">reliable</span> (free from misaligned supervision) and <span id="S3.SS2.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">informative</span> (rich in semantic-ambiguous yet executable behaviors).
The effectiveness of the refinement module is analyzed in §<a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ HATS: Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis for GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, where multi-round replay is shown to monotonically increase action-level recall and substantially improve downstream task success.
As visualized in Fig. <a href="#S3.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 3.1 Hardness-Driven Exploration Module ‣ 3 Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis ‣ HATS: Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis for GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, iterative refinement transforms vague one-shot instructions into precise and executable task instructions, bridging the gap between textual goals and GUI-level actions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S3.T2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:129%;">WebArena evaluation results across website domains. All values are success rates (%).</span></figcaption>
<table id="S3.T2.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S3.T2.7.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.7.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S3.T2.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Base Model</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.7.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" rowspan="2"><span id="S3.T2.7.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Strategies</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.7.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" colspan="4"><span id="S3.T2.7.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">WebArena (Success Rate %)</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.7.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.7.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column">
<span id="S3.T2.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S3.T2.7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T2.7.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Gitlab</span></span>
