</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Closed-Loop Integration</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This stage corresponds to the <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Backpropagation</span> phase of HD-MCTS,
where the alignment scores of refined trajectories are converted into a
unified hardness feedback signal that guides subsequent exploration.
In contrast to conventional MCTS, which backpropagates environment-provided task rewards, GUI trajectory synthesis exposes no such scalar supervision.
We therefore propagate an <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">alignment-derived hardness reward</span> that quantifies semantic difficulty and serves as a task-adaptive surrogate objective.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">I. Motivation and Design of the Hardness Reward.</span> The core idea is to turn semantic misalignment, typically noisy supervision, into informative feedback that prioritizes ambiguous or hard regions of the GUI state space. During refinement, we compute the <span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">action-level reconstruction recall</span> <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A,B)</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 3.2 Alignment-Guided Refinement Module ‣ 3 Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis ‣ HATS: Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis for GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), which measures how well a synthesized instruction <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> reproduces its reference sequence <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. High recall indicates clear semantic grounding, whereas low recall reflects ambiguous visual cues, missing preconditions, or unstable language–interface mappings. Thus, <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> naturally serves as an empirical estimate of <span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">task hardness</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Building on this insight, we define the <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">hardness reward</span> as an inverse function of <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(A,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(A,B)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(A,B)=(R(A,B)+\epsilon)^{-\alpha},\quad\epsilon&gt;0,\ \alpha&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(A,B)=(R(A,B)+\epsilon)^{-\alpha},\quad\epsilon&gt;0,\ \alpha&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This formulation (i) yields a continuous, bounded score that increases smoothly as alignment deteriorates, and
(ii) directly links exploration to the weakest regions of instruction–execution understanding.
We additionally clip hardness into a stable range (e.g., <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,H_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,H_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>) to avoid extreme values.
Within HD-MCTS, this reward replaces task-return signals and encourages revisiting trajectories that are hard to align yet semantically valuable.
We use the default configuration <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon{=}0.01,\ \alpha{=}1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon{=}0.01,\ \alpha{=}1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and analyze parameter sensitivity in §<a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ HATS: Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis for GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">II. Hardness Propagation.</span>
After refinement, each verified instruction–trajectory pair <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I,B)</annotation></semantics></math> yields a hardness value <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(A,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(A,B)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We backpropagate this reward along the <span id="S3.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">tree-policy path</span> from the expansion node to the root:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(v,a)\!\leftarrow\!N(v,a)+1,\ Q(v,a)\!\leftarrow\!Q(v,a)+\tfrac{r-Q(v,a)}{N(v,a)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(v,a)\!\leftarrow\!N(v,a)+1,\ Q(v,a)\!\leftarrow\!Q(v,a)+\tfrac{r-Q(v,a)}{N(v,a)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Following standard MCTS, only nodes selected by the tree policy receive credit.
Since hardness characterizes the entire instruction–trajectory pair rather than any single action,
the same scalar reward is propagated along the path. These updates reshape the value estimates,
biasing future UCB selection (Eq. <a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 3.1 Hardness-Driven Exploration Module ‣ 3 Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis ‣ HATS: Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis for GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) toward semantically challenging regions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, the closed loop of <span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HATS</span> turns semantic ambiguity from a training liability into a useful learning signal. Misalignment during replay generates the hardness reward, which in turn guides exploration toward richer and harder-to-align interactions. <span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Verified trajectories</span> annotated with hardness form a semantically grounded dataset for downstream SFT training. We follow the two-stage paradigm of <span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">OS-Genesis</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite> for planning-level and action-level learning, with hardness-aware weighting detailed in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ HATS: Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis for GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S3.T3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:129%;">Parameter sensitivity of the hardness reward in Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ 3.3 Closed-Loop Integration ‣ 3 Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis ‣ HATS: Hardness-Aware Trajectory Synthesis for GUI Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S3.T3.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S3.T3.7.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T3.7.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:134.2pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T3.7.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Hardness Metric</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S3.T3.7.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;" colspan="2"><span id="S3.T3.7.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Hyperparameters</span></th>
<th id="S3.T3.7.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:146.6pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T3.7.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Success Rate (%)</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S3.T3.7.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T3.7.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"></th>
<th id="S3.T3.7.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:64.6pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S3.T3.7.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:64.6pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝜶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S3.T3.7.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column" style="padding-bottom: 2.0pt;padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S3.T3.7.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T3.7.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:134.2pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R(A,B)+\epsilon)^{-\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">B</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">ϵ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">α</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R(A,B)+\epsilon)^{-\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></th>
<td id="S3.T3.7.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:64.6pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T3.7.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">0.01</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T3.7.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:64.6pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T3.7.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">0.50</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T3.7.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.3.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:146.6pt;">
<span id="S3.T3.7.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.T3.7.3.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">22.7 </span><span id="S3.T3.7.3.4.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">-55.3%</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
